1
00:00:00,661 --> 00:00:07,906
This is Broker Order Desk: a complete brokerage platform, with a
React dashboard on a Spring Boot backend, written in Java twenty

2
00:00:07,906 --> 00:00:15,151
five. It covers trading, margin, charts, analytics, news,
wallet, alerts, liquidity providers, and an administrator's

3
00:00:15,151 --> 00:00:18,774
audit trail. Everything is synthetic.

4
00:00:20,233 --> 00:00:27,033
The header is live. Market state, a synthetic index with its
trend, breadth, and session totals. A server push stream updates

5
00:00:27,033 --> 00:00:33,834
every screen the moment an order or a trade happens, with
polling only as a safety net.

6
00:00:34,438 --> 00:00:41,921
The price board shows offer and bid from the real order book,
last price, trades, average, volume, value, high, low, a trend

7
00:00:41,921 --> 00:00:49,404
line, and the change. Hover a symbol for its daily limits.
Favorites, sorting, and an export to C S V.

8
00:00:50,005 --> 00:00:57,267
Investor two sells twenty thousand shares at twelve riyals and
five hundred mills. Pre trade risk reserves those shares, and

9
00:00:57,267 --> 00:01:00,898
the order rests in the book. The depth panel shows it.

10
00:01:03,226 --> 00:01:10,926
Investor one buys the same size. The engine matches by price and
time, and the trade settles in one database transaction. The

11
00:01:10,926 --> 00:01:18,627
balance turned negative: that is the margin loan, and equity is
forty percent, above the maintenance level.

12
00:01:20,941 --> 00:01:28,109
The price moves. Investor two offers five thousand shares at
eleven riyals three hundred, inside the daily band.

13
00:01:33,318 --> 00:01:39,249
Investor one buys a thousand. The position is marked to market,
equity drops below maintenance, and the flag turns red: margin

14
00:01:39,249 --> 00:01:42,214
call.

15
00:01:42,819 --> 00:01:47,019
The margin screen shows it on a gauge, with the needle inside
the red zone.

16
00:01:47,624 --> 00:01:54,782
In the wallet, a withdrawal is refused: the margin loan has to
be repaid first. A withdrawal can never reach into borrowed

17
00:01:54,782 --> 00:02:01,939
money. A deposit through a bank rail credits the account exactly
once, even if the request is retried.

18
00:02:02,544 --> 00:02:09,306
Investor one sets a price alert. It fires once, when a trade
prints through the target, and pops up on screen.

19
00:02:09,907 --> 00:02:16,083
Charts. Candlesticks with volume for any symbol or the index,
with ranges from one month to all. Compare mode puts several

20
00:02:16,083 --> 00:02:22,259
symbols on one axis, as percentage change since the start of the
range.

21
00:02:22,864 --> 00:02:29,885
Analytics. Statements and ratios per company: assets,
liabilities, equity, profit, earnings per share, dividend yield,

22
00:02:29,885 --> 00:02:36,907
book value, price to earnings, and price to book. Computed live
from the last price, and covered by unit tests, including losses

23
00:02:36,907 --> 00:02:40,418
and zero denominators.

24
00:02:41,022 --> 00:02:45,182
News and disclosures, market wide or per company, next to the
chart.

25
00:02:45,786 --> 00:02:50,116
The whole interface switches to Arabic with a right to left
layout, in one click.

26
00:02:51,884 --> 00:02:59,364
Back in English. Three pre trade checks. A price outside the
daily band is rejected. An order bigger than the buying power is

27
00:02:59,364 --> 00:03:03,104
rejected. Selling shares you do not own is rejected.

28
00:03:05,402 --> 00:03:12,144
Investor two cancels the resting order. The engine removes it
from the book and releases the reserved shares.

29
00:03:14,468 --> 00:03:22,084
The liquidity provider posts a two sided quote through the same
risk and matching path as any order. The activity chart shows

30
00:03:22,084 --> 00:03:25,892
liquidity provider trades apart from ordinary market trades.

31
00:03:26,497 --> 00:03:33,934
Services. The margin terms come straight from the live rules.
The institutions tab says plainly what is built, and what is

32
00:03:33,934 --> 00:03:37,653
not: a FIX gateway and direct market access are not.

33
00:03:39,969 --> 00:03:46,556
The administrator reviews the audit trail, and the account
applications that arrived from the public open account form.

34
00:03:47,159 --> 00:03:53,834
Forty four automated tests stand behind this, including a
concurrency stress test proving cash and shares are conserved,

35
00:03:53,834 --> 00:04:00,509
and a failure test where the database drops in the middle of
settlement. A benchmark compares garbage collectors for the

36
00:04:00,509 --> 00:04:07,184
matching path, and the container runs on the one that cut the
long pauses tenfold. There is a Dockerfile, Kubernetes

37
00:04:07,184 --> 00:04:13,860
manifests, a CI pipeline, specs and a changelog, and the code is
in the Git repository.
